  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>When glucose is treated with dilute&nbsp;NaOH, it&nbsp;gives a&nbsp;mixture of&nbsp;D-glucose,&nbsp;D-mannose and&nbsp;D-fructose. This reaction is known as Lobry de Bruyn-van Ekenstein rearrangement.&nbsp;Basic catalysed&nbsp;tautomerism through enediol intermediate takes place.<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/99e94215-b97f-42e3-8b9e-1ab813c44005-image.png\" style=\"width: 508px; height: 450px;\" /></p></blockquote>",
